Subject: Cantor M2B Supplied Root Topology Projection Justification

& [JustificationIdentity] is traceable
  + [justification_uuid] is a2c370cc-8a1d-4da4-8c45-0b0296740eb8
  + [profile] is cantor-windows-supplied-root-topology-projection/0.1
  + [source_snapshot_uuid] is b633f2a2-35f1-44ec-b37d-a9de93525c6e

& [Claim] a distinct revalidated supplied root carrier should precede mixed inventory
  + M2A root semantics differ from descendant directory semantics
  + current preflight form carries supplied root identity and path syntax
  + current stability authority supplies revalidated directory metadata
  + exact identity and component joins detect supplied graph disagreement
  + mixed inventory needs a root carrier to preserve complete lineage
  + physical production remains a larger separate authority boundary

& [Selection] is strict plan plus complete preflight and stability inputs
  + rerun both current validators
  + accept only eligible CompleteLocal
  + require exact reference, complete strong identity, and dual final-component equality
  + fix root kind, directory mode, no path, no content, and ordinal 1
  + preserve every complete input and the current-M2A-valid form in an output-only wrapper
  + reject descendant-as-root, bare fragments, physical production, inventory, Git, receipt, and admission

& [Counterarguments] are answered
  + a valid preflight record is not runtime proof because the public enum is constructible and deserializable
  + repeating pure validation is justified because it makes the current construction path explicit
  + exact identity and component equality is useful inconsistency detection but not physical correspondence
  + rejecting a drive root is required by the current component-policy mismatch and does not narrow the earlier preflight authority itself
  + fixed ordinal 1 is a structural root convention and must not be described as traversal observation

& [RiskBalance] reduces forged lower success, descendant/root conflation, field invention, validation drift, and provenance inflation while retaining the declared risk that callers can supply coherent fictional values

& [Decision] proceed only under a distinct satisfaction signature for one pure module and in-memory tests; physical and downstream authority remain absent
